# Where the functions are in a file that does not say.
#
# This is not a tidiness feature. Every analysis in the pipeline is
# per-function, so a "function" that is really the whole of .text glued
# together has flags written in one function reaching a read in the next:
# nothing is dead, nothing folds, and the listing degenerates into the raw
# CF/OF/SF/PF arithmetic Sleigh emits for every instruction. Bounding the
# functions is what makes a readable listing possible at all.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: echo 'static int helper(int a, int b) { return a * b + 7; }' > %t/p.c
# RUN: echo 'int compute(int n) { int t = 0; for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) t += helper(i, n); return t; }' >> %t/p.c
# RUN: echo 'int main(void) { return compute(5); }' >> %t/p.c
# RUN: gcc -O0 -no-pie -o %t/p %t/p.c
# RUN: strip %t/p

# Stripped: the container knows nothing about functions any more.
# RUN: %sleigh-poc --file=%t/p --specs=%specs --functions 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=STRIPPED %s

# STRIPPED: 0 function(s)


# But something calls them, and a call survives stripping. Each one is bounded
# by control flow -- the last address reachable from its entry -- so it stops
# where the function does rather than running on into the next one.
#
# RUN: printf 'functions\nquit\n' \
# RUN:   | %sleigh-poc --file=%t/p --specs=%specs --project=%t/none.ddd --server \
# RUN:   2>/dev/null | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND %s

# FOUND: {"functions":[{"addr":
# FOUND-SAME: "name":"sub_

# The whole executable segment is thousands of bytes; a discovered function is
# a function, so its size has at most three digits here.
# FOUND-SAME: "size":{{[0-9][0-9]?[0-9]?,}}


# And the listing of one is the function, not the segment: it ends at a return
# rather than running into whatever was laid out next.
#
# RUN: %sleigh-poc --file=%t/p --specs=%specs --project=%t/none.ddd \
# RUN:   --region=0x400000:0x401000:x86-64 --raw --base=0x400000 2>/dev/null \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NOISE %s

# The flag dance Sleigh emits for a compare must not survive into the listing:
# with the function correctly bounded, the parity flag is dead and everything
# feeding it goes with it.
# NOISE-NOT: POPCOUNT
# NOISE-NOT: PF =
